{
  "about": "Shared test vectors for team chat, read by desktop (test/chat-vectors.test.js and the chat-wire and chat-text tests) and Android (Utf8OffsetsTest, InviteLinkTest, Uuid7Test) where the file is. Every ID, secret and name is made up. mentions: text with the same mentions as UTF-16 code unit ranges (utf16, what the editors hold) and UTF-8 byte ranges (bytes, the wire form); bytes[k].start equals the UTF-8 length of text.slice(0, utf16[k].start). badMentions: byte ranges that break exactly one wire rule, named in rule: split_character (a start or end inside a character), out_of_order (starts before the previous mention starts), overlap (starts before the previous one ends), past_end, empty (end not after start), too_many (more than 32), bad_actor (not u_ plus 22 base64url characters). Touching ranges are allowed. inviteLinks: text pasted by the person and server, the configured account server; expect is { server, workspace, secret } or null, error is null, bad_link or other_server. Characters that can't end a link (. , ; : ! ? ) ] } > ' \" and the typographic quotes) are dropped from its end, and a link without https:// or http:// is read as https (contract section 3.2). android, when present, replaces expect and error on Android in the named build. uuidv7: ms and 10 random bytes as hex give id with the layout of contract section 3.8.",
